    {
      "id": "N02",
      "lead": [
        {
          "text": "In its most recent statements, the bank has emphasized the importance of wage growth and inflation expectations in determining the future path of policy.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "resourceId": "basis-yen-strength-and-the-rate-differential-implications-for-inve",
              "version": "v1",
              "spanId": "p3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Bank of Japan has repeatedly indicated that it won't hesitate to ease further if needed, but it has also acknowledged that the side effects of prolonged easing are becoming more visible.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "resourceId": "basis-yen-strength-and-the-rate-differential-implications-for-inve",
              "version": "v1",
              "spanId": "p3"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answersIt": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "N03",
      "lead": [
        {
          "text": "The problem is that Singapore's home loan market is structurally allergic to rate rises, and almost nobody is prepared.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "resourceId": "kopi-singapore-home-loans-the-silent-rate-sensitivity-killer",
              "version": "v1",
              "spanId": "p2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Two years, maybe three, then you are dumped into a floating rate that tracks SORA or some bank's internal board rate, which is a polite way of saying \"whatever we feel like.\" The banks know this.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "resourceId": "kopi-singapore-home-loans-the-silent-rate-sensitivity-killer",
              "version": "v1",
              "spanId": "p3"
